Well, you have to understand that Nethack is open source software for
a reason.

These days, the Dev Team seems to be functioning primarily as a
gatekeeper for user-created patches.  This isn't to imply that they
don't add new features themselves, or that they don't fix bugs (one
look at the bug listing on the site makes it clear they do a lot of
work there), but that most of the new features that make it into the
game seem to be things that get coded as outside patches first, and
are then are judged worthy of incorporation into the main game.

In other words, the best way to get your feature into the game is to
code it yourself, or post a YANI that attracts the eye of a programmer
with the will and energy to implement (which doesn't seem to happen
*too* often), and then, if it's obvious that the patch really enhances
the game, and doesn't break it in a way it should be broken (a lot of
*current* Nethack features would look like bad ideas to a traditional
game developer), you may find that the next version of Nethack will
have your modification included.

Note: I have no communication with the Dev Team and claim no special
insight into their processes.  But I'm guessing that this is mostly
how it goes these days.  People with more experience here, feel free
to correct/contradict me.

